      "maphelp.cross": "Locate & crosshair. Tap to cycle: off → GPS-follow (keeps the map on your position) → read-cursor (the fixed centre cross reads whatever dot sits under it — an observation, map point or eBird hotspot — and shows its popup). Press-and-hold (or right-click) to recall your saved locations and fly to one.",
      "maphelp.nearby": "Close by. Opens a list of the nearest plotted detections (and, if enabled, your map points), sorted by distance from the live/fixed crosshair or a placed pin. Tap a row to fly there.",
      "maphelp.search": "Place search. Type at least two letters to fuzzy-search place names (recent searches are listed too). Press-and-hold to recall your saved locations and fly to one.",
      "maphelp.offline": "Offline maps. Download the current view's map tiles so the area works with no connection. Press-and-hold (or right-click) to open the manager — downloaded areas show as coloured frames with an × to delete, and the app re-offers a download if the browser evicts them. Downloaded areas don't count against the map-tile cache.",
      "maphelp.legend": "Legend. The plotted species, ordered by the model's predicted probability (low → high). Top buttons: − minimise to a corner chip; ☰ open the detections list (where the time, species and observer filters live); a black × clears the active filters (long-press or right-click it to open a panel of every filter, showing which are active); a red × removes every plotted detection (arms per-area delete when fetched-area outlines exist); ⚠ appears when the draw cap (Settings → Max points) is hiding dots. The list shows only species with a dot on screen; the number after each is how many of its specimens are on screen (passing the filters), and the top “Total” row sums that across all species (n of the grand total). Tap a species row to toggle it on/off — picks stack, so several show together; hover a row to isolate that species on the map.",
      "maphelp.detlist": "Detections list. A large-text list of the plotted detections, sorted by time (grouped by date & observer) or by species, 2nd-language name, count or rarity. Its filter row holds the time window (days / weeks / months, a from–to range and month-of-year chips), the species filter (★ starred · ◉ locally rare · 🟡 not on this year's list · 🔴 not on your life list) and the 👤 observer filter. A fuzzy species search appears once the list is long; while searching, “Select on map” adds the matches to the legend. Each row's 🎯 flies the map to that record; tapping a row opens its species menu. “Save as list” and “Navigate” build a route through the points.",
